# Copy to `.env` and edit. Compose reads `.env` automatically, so every
# `docker compose` command in this directory picks these up — unlike a one-off
# `VAR=x docker compose up`, which applies to that single command and lets the
# NEXT one recreate the container without it.
#
# `.env` is gitignored. This example file is not, so it must never hold a real
# secret.

# eiermann's port, everywhere. federfall's dev stack owns 8090, and the app's
# development defines (apps/eiermann/dart_defines/development.json) point at
# 8091 — keep the two in agreement or the app cannot find its own backend.
EIERMANN_PORT=8091

# The first user. Without these a fresh instance has no way in: a PocketBase
# superuser is not an app-level coordinator. Idempotent, and also the
# lockout-recovery path. Clear them once the team exists.
EIERMANN_COORDINATOR_EMAIL=dev@eiermann.local
EIERMANN_COORDINATOR_PASSWORD=DevPass12345!
EIERMANN_COORDINATOR_NAME=Koordination

# ── The geocoder ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Both of these want setting before a real deployment, and neither does
# anything in development. Empty means the public OSM Nominatim under the
# User-Agent "eiermann/1.0", and that instance blocks application backends and
# placeholder agents — so address lookup works on your laptop and stops the day
# somebody else uses it. Self-host, or put a real contact in the agent.
#
# EIERMANN_NOMINATIM_URL=https://nominatim.example.org
# EIERMANN_USER_AGENT=eiermann/1.0 (tauben@example.org)

# ── The map source ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ALL OR NOTHING: /api/eiermann/info refuses a partial set and the app falls
# back to its build-time defines, because a half-applied override naming the
# wrong provider is a licensing problem. Set the mode, the URL for that mode,
# and the credit the provider requires.
#
# EIERMANN_MAP_MODE=raster
# EIERMANN_MAP_TILE_URL=https://tiles.example.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png
# EIERMANN_MAP_ATTRIBUTION=© OpenStreetMap-Mitwirkende
# EIERMANN_MAP_ATTRIBUTION_URL=https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
